## 5. Global generation blocks (for the b-roll generator / shoot)

**Positive base — append to every shot prompt.**
> A realistic editorial diary photograph of the same fictional North Indian woman, age 22–26, wheatish skin with natural texture, long open dark hair worn fully down, a small centred maroon bindi, and silver jhumkas. Warm daylight, modest opaque everyday [wardrobe], [activity] in [non-intimate setting], neutral eye-level medium framing, natural posture, realistic skin texture, respectful lifestyle editorial. Include a clearly readable on-image disclosure: “AI-generated”.

**Exclusion block — append to every shot prompt (Persona Bible §3, unmodified).**
> Do not change her face, apparent age, complexion, hairline, or facial proportions. No tied hair, braid, ponytail, bun, clip-up, or updo. No missing maroon bindi or silver jhumkas. No glamorised or sexualised styling; no sheer, tight, low-cut, strapless, wet, lingerie-like, or bodycon clothing. No seductive pose/expression, reclining, bedroom/bathroom/bed setting, body-focused crop, low-angle chest/hip emphasis, or suggestive copy. No absent, hidden, cropped out, illegible, or low-contrast AI-generated disclosure.

**Anchor binding.** Feed the registered crop for the post’s anchor ID as the
identity reference on every generation, and add the registered SHA-256 to the
QA record so continuity is provable, not asserted.

